# What `railway up` must not try to index.
#
# The repo-root .gitignore already lists these, but `railway up` runs from inside server/
# (the CLI has no --root-directory flag), so an ignore file one level above its upload root
# is never consulted. This file is that ignore, at the root the CLI actually uses.
#
# `.pytest-tmp/` is the one that matters: a pytest --basetemp left behind unreadable even to
# its owner. A directory the indexer cannot scandir is an EPERM, not a skip, so it fails the
# whole deploy with "Access is denied. (os error 5)" and names nothing.

# pytest basetemp leftovers — hyphenated, so .dockerignore's `.pytest_cache/` misses them
.pytest-tmp/
.pytest-run-next/
.pytest_cache/

# Build / cache artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

